  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN vertices.\nVertex iii has the integer AiA_iAi​ written on it. It is guaranteed that Ai≠0A_i \\ne 0Ai​=0.\n\nA walk in the tree is a sequence of vertices (x1,x2,…,xk)(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_k)(x1​,x2​,…,xk​) such that there exists an edge between xix_ixi​ and xi+1x_{i+1}xi+1​ for each 1≤i&lt;k1 \\le i \\lt k1≤i&lt;k.\n\nThe length of such a walk is said to be kkk.\nNote that in particular, it is allowed for vertices to repeat in a walk.\n\nThe score of a walk is defined as follows:\n\n\nStart with P=1P = 1P=1.\nThen, for each i=1,2,3,…,ki = 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, ki=1,2,3,…,k in order, update PPP using the following rules:\n\nIf vertex xix_ixi​ has appeared before in the walk, do nothing.\n\nThat is, each vertex must only be processed the first time it's seen.\nOtherwise, let w=Axiw = A_{x_i}w=Axi​​ be the value at the current vertex. Then,\n\nIf w&gt;0w \\gt 0w&gt;0, multiply PPP by 2w2^{w}2w.\nIf w&lt;0w \\lt 0w&lt;0, multiply PPP by −2−w-2^{-w}−2−w.\n\n\n\n\nThe score of the walk is then the final value of PPP, after all kkk vertices have been processed.\nYour task is to compute the maximum possible score of a walk in the tree. The walk can start and end at any vertex, and have any positive length (in particular it's allowed to start and end at the same vertex without moving).\n\nThe answer can be large, so report it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of vertices.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the values written on the vertices.\nThe next N−1N - 1N−1 lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these N−1N - 1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer: the maximum possible score of a walk in the graph, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\le A_i \\le 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "Ai≠0A_i \\ne 0Ai​=0",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The input graph is a tree on {1,2,…,N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}{1,2,…,N}.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
